                          "name": "Python integers become torch.int64, Pyth",
                          "content": "Python integers become torch.int64, Python floats torch.float32, a NumPy float64 array stays float64. A reduction like .sum() gives a 0-d tensor, torch.Size([]) — call .item() to get a Python number. Tensors start on the CPU until you .to(device).",
